        <mxCell id="c252" value="&lt;i&gt;Report view, page Refund Ranking, in a different arrangement from the model answer&#x27;s (the page also holds a text box with the written answer, not drawn). The bars count the refunds at scores 0 to 5: 4, 18, 53, 83, 44, 20. The matrix totals the flags: its Total row is blank because the flag measures switch on one selected flag, and its Total column (outlined in teal, like the Score column of the table) is the sum of the years. The 64 refunds scoring 4 or 5 (80,776.86) are the first to review. The table lists all 222 refunds, 8 in view, sorted by score and then amount; the first row, RF-2026-000205, is selected (outlined in blue) before a reviewer drills through to its detail. The largest refund, RF-2025-000097, scores 4 and is not at the top. The headings of the flags are broken over two lines to fit.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontColor=#5D6D7E;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacing=2;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="758" width="860" height="83" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
